      "title": "CFE in health emergencies",
      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-cfe-in-health-emergencies.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The CFE enabled WHO to mount rapid and sustained \nresponses to 14 separate emergencies in 13 countries \nand one global response (COVID-19) in 2020. A total \nof nearly US$ 44 million was released in 2020. Table 1 \ncontains a list of all approved releases by event in 2020.\nSome 80% of funding released from the CFE went to \nsupport just three events in 2020: the two Ebola outbreaks \nin the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) and the \nCOVID-19 global response. These emergencies also",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Reports that in 2020 the fund supported responses to 14 emergencies in 13 countries plus COVID-19, releasing nearly US$ 44 million, with about 80% going to COVID-19 and to two Ebola outbreaks in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
