      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-006-expenditures.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "last year.\nIn 2020, the CFE continued to support critical, life-saving \noperations in response to the Ebola outbreak in North \nKivu, DRC, which started in 2018. In their 2020 annual \nreport to the World Health Assembly the External Auditor \nnoted that the use of the CFE to bridge funding gaps in \nthe protracted Ebola outbreak was outside the scope \nof the Fund but accepted the Secretariat’s explanation \nregarding the exceptional circumstances.1 The CFE’s \nexceptional prolonged use in the North Kivu outbreak was \nnecessary in the absence of sufficient donor funding for \nthe response. The CFE wa",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Details 2020 fund expenditures, including bridging funding gaps in the protracted North Kivu Ebola response, US$ 5.3 million for the Equateur Ebola outbreak and US$ 12.9 million for early COVID-19 response. It lists other emergencies supported, reports that most small allocations were released within 24 hours, and gives a table of releases by event and a chart of refund rates by year.",
