        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Replenishing the CFE",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 13,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-replenishing-the-cfe.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The CFE was conceived by Member States and launched \nin 2015 as a revolving fund. Costs initially incurred against \nCFE allocations would be reimbursed by donor funding to \nthe WHO emergency response at country level and unspent \nfunds would be returned. In practice, it has proven difficult \nto raise the level of resources required at country level \nto sustainably replenish the CFE in this manner.\nIn 2020, approximately 40% of CFE allocations were \nrefunded (as at 22 April 2021). While low, it was higher \nthan in previous years (except for 2018). Figure 2 shows \nthe refund rate by year.\nThe re",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that the fund was designed to be revolving but has been hard to replenish, with about 40% of 2020 allocations refunded. It notes that refunds vary by emergency, with most COVID-19 releases reimbursed but Ebola releases less so, and presents a table of releases and refunds by event.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
