      "target": "../sections/sec-008-cfe-contributions.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In 2020, 13 Member States generously made contributions \nto the CFE totaling almost US$ 23 million (Table 3). \nAustria joined the list of contributors for the first time. \nContributions dropped from the previous two years. \nThis was likely to be as a result of the exceptional focus \nlast year on addressing and fully funding the COVID-19 \nresponse (Figure 3). See Annex 3 for a complete list \nof CFE contributors since 2015.\nTable 3  CFE contributions in 2020\nCountry\nContribution (US$)\nNetherlands\n 6 794 448 \nGermany\n 4 506 001 \nSweden\n 4 186 545 \nNorway\n 2 580 461 \nCanada\n 1 455 592 \nDenmark\n 1",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Reports that 13 Member States contributed nearly US$ 23 million in 2020, down from previous years likely because of the focus on funding COVID-19, with Austria joining for the first time. Tables and a chart show contributions by country and for 2015–2020, and the block notes how the fund enabled rapid responses amid multiple crises.",
